{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1518019529,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyOTUxOTQ1MjE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2124","origin":"github"},"title":"mishandling of git-annex external special remote protocol unsupported request","message":"To use new special remote protocol messages like the one added in\nhttp://git-annex.branchable.com/todo/INFO_message_for_custom_special_remotes/ , external special remotes need a way to determine if git-annex supports the command. http://git-annex.branchable.com/design/external_special_remote_protocol has a plan to make git-annex send a new message after VERSION indicating its capabilities.\n\nOn auditing all external special remotes to see if they will work well with such a new message, I found all did, except for the one in datalad, which does this:\n\n            method = getattr(self, \"req_%s\" % req, None)\n            if not method:\n                self.error(\"We have no support for %s request, part of %s response\"\n                           % (req, l))\n                self.send(\"UNSUPPORTED-REQUEST\")\n                continue\n\nAs far as I can tell, this probably crashes. It should simply send back the UNSUPPORTED-REQUEST and let git-annex deal with it.","files":null}]}